 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so we got the green light from the client (regional insurance co) to build a claims-intake agent — customer uploads photos + describes the incident, agent pulls the policy from their Guidewire API, triages severity, and either auto-approves small stuff or routes to an adjuster. we're planning ADK on Cloud Run, probably Gemini for the vision part. Team is me + one other dev + a part-time designer, and they want something demo-able in 6 weeks. Can you help me figure out what actually goes in v1 vs later phases, and sketch the architecture (single agent vs multi-agent, where state lives, how we handle the human handoff)? I'd rather argue about this now than refactor in week 4."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Need to turn our design for an internal IT helpdesk agent into a statement of work for the client. Scope: ADK agent on Vertex AI Agent Engine, integrates with ServiceNow + Google Workspace admin, handles password resets, license requests, FAQ via RAG over their Confluence. Help me structure the SOW — phases, deliverables, assumptions, what's explicitly out of scope, rough effort per phase. Formal tone, they're a bank."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "our ADK agent on Agent Engine keeps timing out when it calls the ServiceNow tool — works fine locally with adk web but in prod every call over ~30s just dies with a DeadlineExceeded. architecture's already settled, just need this fixed before thursday's demo", "needs_instead": "Debugging a deployed agent's runtime/tool-call timeout issue in production, not upfront requirements, architecture planning, or proposal writing."}
